abstract: >-
  On the periodic torus (Z/LZ)^4, for 0 <= beta <= 0.81348 (Wilson action, beta = 4/g^2), every planar rectangular Wilson loop of the
  four-dimensional SU(2) lattice gauge theory with sides R <= L/2 and T <= L-1 satisfies |<W>| <= C^T theta^(RT), with explicit constants
  theta < 1 and C independent of L; the string tension is positive. The proof follows the method of Borgs and Seiler (1983,
  Appendix B), whose threshold is beta < 12/17, and refines it (12/17 to 0.81348, +15.2%) with a strict operator inequality and a
  transfer matrix of memory 11 on 7 821 056 symmetry classes, bounded by an integer Perron certificate; every numerical inequality is
  verified in exact integer or rational arithmetic. The result is computer-assisted, holds on tori only, and has been checked by
  machine only (independent programs, reviews by language models, and a partial formalisation in Lean that assumes the analytic
  reduction), not by a human referee.
